# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — repository root .gitignore
#
# READ THIS BEFORE EDITING: git applies the LAST matching rule. A broad pattern written
# after a re-include silently re-ignores the files you just rescued, and the file reads
# top-to-bottom while behaving bottom-to-top. Any re-include block therefore stays at the
# very END of this file. Verify a specific path with `git check-ignore -v <path>`, which
# names the winning rule and its line number, instead of reading and guessing.
# (docs/GOTCHAS.md)

########################################
# OS / editor noise
########################################
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.swp
.idea/
.vs/

########################################
# Agent tooling
########################################
# Working copies created by agent tools: full checkouts, never repository content.
# Add your tools' own scratch directories here; an overlay may bring more.
.claude/worktrees/
# A Codex worker's decision files (spawn_codex.sh): QUESTION-NAME.md, or FILE.question.md
# beside a --result FILE. Result reports stay visible for the lead's review; close_worker.sh
# moves the default RESULT-NAME.md under .myagentkit/workers/, beside the worker's records.
/QUESTION-*.md
*.md.question.md
# The private store in any case: Windows and macOS fold case, so `.MYAGENTKIT/` is the same
# folder, and with core.ignorecase false a lowercase-only rule let `git add -A` stage it.
/.[Mm][Yy][Aa][Gg][Ee][Nn][Tt][Kk][Ii][Tt]/
# Backend credentials live outside the repository (docs/DEV_SETUP.md, section 3); the old
# in-repository place is read while projects move, so it stays ignored and untracked.
/.myagentkit/backends/
# Raw review evidence holds the whole diff and the reviewing CLI's own output. It stays
# local; publish a deliberately scrubbed `-summary.md` instead (re-included at the bottom).
/docs/reviews/????????T??????Z-*.md
/docs/handoffs/*-claude-propose.json
# Legacy name from before every reviewer shared one Markdown format.
/docs/reviews/*-claude-review.json

# Local-only tool settings. Shared configuration is committed; per-machine overrides
# and anything holding a credential are not.
*/settings.local.json

########################################
# Stack-specific rules
########################################
# {{STACK_IGNORE_RULES}} — replace this ENTIRE line, leading "#" included, with the
# stack's rules. A half-edit that keeps the "#" ships an ignore line that ignores nothing,
# and the build junk it was meant to stop lands in the next commit.

########################################
# Re-includes — MUST STAY LAST (git applies the last matching rule)
########################################
# Hand-written project files that a broad pattern above would otherwise swallow go here,
# and nowhere else.
!/docs/reviews/*-summary.md
